 "title": "OMP 18.3.5 live steering over the openai-responses route: no abort, delivered as the next stateful turn",
 "generated_utc": "2026-09-28T04:43:47Z",
 "status": "observed",
 "question": "When an operator steers unmodified OMP 18.3.5 while it streams from the lane over the documented openai-responses provider, does OMP abort the in-flight response, and how does the steer reach the server?",
 "answer": "It does not abort. The first response streamed to response.completed with its full answer, and 27 ms later OMP sent the steer as a new streamed request whose previous_response_id was that response's id and whose only input item was the steer's user message; the model answered the steer exactly. The lane sees an ordinary stateful continuation, never a cancelled stream.",
